", "url": "https://www.boxofficemojo.com/release/rl1235846657/weekend"}, {"title": "Tickets IMAX Donate", "url": "https://tnaqua.org/?p=9067"}, {"title": "E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial", "url": "https://kaweah.freedombox.rocks/kiwix/wikipedia_en_all_maxi_2023-10/E.T."}, {"title": "today in film history june 11th 1982 e t the extra terrestrial is released in theaters", "url": "https://www.westporttechmuseum.com/blogs/techtastic/today-in-film-history-june-11th-1982-e-t-the-extra-terrestrial-is-released-in-theaters"}, {"title": "e t the extra terrestrial", "url": "https://thefridacinema.org/movies/e-t-the-extra-terrestrial/"}, {"title": "Checked content", "url": "https://solarspell-dls.sfis.asu.edu/mea/wikipedia/wp/e/E.T._the_Extra-Terrestrial.htm"}]}, "The film's U.S. theatrical release was **June 11, 1982**, distributed by Universal Pictures. Its earlier festival premiere was **May 26, 1982**, at Cannes.\n\n- **Cannes premiere:** A Wikipedia mirror lists the Cannes date and notes the film closed that festival (a 1982 American science fiction film produced and directed by Steven Spielberg; premiered as the closing film of the Cannes Film Festival on May 26, 1982). A film-history blog gives the same date.\n- **U.S. release:** Several sources, including a 2022 IMAX re-release article, give June 11, 1982 as the debut date in theaters.\n- **Reliability:** Some results were low-quality pages (e.g., a university jobs subdomain and a generic SEO-style page), so I relied mainly on the Wikipedia mirror and the blog and press items, which agree on both dates."], "durationSeconds": 6.159558542, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01Xoa8KVDy5vSLinmdiZgyUY", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01TxAEsKxe8es2qTNaCka6c3", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweets_from_a_Stranger\"}, {\"url\": \"https://powerpop.blog/tag/squeeze/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://medialoper.com/tag/squeeze/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://powerpop.blog/tag/black-coffee-in-bed/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://powerpop.blog/category/1980s/page/11\"}, {\"url\": \"https://music.apple.com/album/1443994094\"}, {\"url\": \"https://cs.uwaterloo.ca/~dtompkin/music/track/SQUEEZE__GH1/SQUEEZE__GH1-11.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://music.apple.com/ca/artist/squeeze/93650\"}, {\"url\": \"https://medialoper.com/certain-songs-2445-squeeze-black-coffee-in-bed/\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:57:11.112Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Squeeze \"Is That Love\" \"Black Coffee in Bed\" \"I Think I'm Go Go\" song release year", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_013V3HzZHeMquLbuc6ezDDWu", "content": [{"title": "Sweets from a Stranger", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweets_from_a_Stranger"}, {"title": "Squeeze – Piccadilly", "url": "https://powerpop.blog/tag/squeeze/"}, {"title": "• Skip to main content", "url": "https://medialoper.com/tag/squeeze/"}, {"title": "Squeeze – Black Coffee In Bed", "url": "https://powerpop.blog/tag/black-coffee-in-bed/"}, {"title": "Squeeze – Black Coffee In Bed", "url": "https://powerpop.blog/category/1980s/page/11"}, {"title": "Sweets from a Stranger", "url": "https://music.apple.com/album/1443994094"}, {"title": "Squeeze Black Coffee in Bed |", "url": "https://cs.uwaterloo.ca/~dtompkin/music/track/SQUEEZE__GH1/SQUEEZE__GH1-11.html"}, {"title": "Latest Release", "url": "https://music.apple.com/ca/artist/squeeze/93650"}, {"title": "• Skip to main content", "url": "https://medialoper.com/certain-songs-2445-squeeze-black-coffee-in-bed/"}]}, "The search confirmed two of the three songs. Nothing came back on \"I Think I'm Go Go.\"\n\n- **\"Black Coffee in Bed\" (1982):** Its single came out in April 1982. Wikipedia lists a release date of 9 April 1982 for it, on the album Sweets from a Stranger. A blog review calls it the lead single from that album.\n- **\"Is That Love\" (1981):** It is a track on the 1981 album East Side Story, which an Apple Music artist profile mentions in its description alongside the band's earlier work. The results don't give a separate single release date, so 1981 reflects the album year, not confirmed single timing.\n- **\"I Think I'm Go Go\":** None of the results mention this song, so I can't give its release year from this search."], "durationSeconds": 7.246567083, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01TxAEsKxe8es2qTNaCka6c3", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
